
# 8. Merge Sort

## Question Description
Implement the Merge Sort algorithm in C++ to sort an array in ascending order. Merge Sort uses the divide-and-conquer technique by dividing the array into smaller parts, sorting them, and merging them.

## Test Cases

### Test Case 1
Input: `[38, 27, 43, 3, 9, 82, 10]`

Expected Output:
`[3, 9, 10, 27, 38, 43, 82]`

### Test Case 2
Input: `[5, 2, 8, 1, 6]`

Expected Output:
`[1, 2, 5, 6, 8]`

### Test Case 3
Input: `[4, 4, 2, 1]`

Expected Output:
`[1, 2, 4, 4]`

## Time Complexity
- Best Case: O(n log n)
- Average Case: O(n log n)
- Worst Case: O(n log n)

## Space Complexity
- O(n)
